        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, Co(acac)2·2H2O (0.29 g, 1.0 mmol) and Y(NO3)3·6H2O (0.38 g, 1.0 mmol) were dissolved in MeOH (20 mL), followed by 6-chloro-2-hydroxypyridine (0.24 g, 2.0 mmol) and triethylamine (0.25 mL, 2.0 mmol), giving a purple solution. After stirring for 6 h, MeOH was removed and the residue was redissolved in MeCN (15 mL) and allowed to evaporate slowly. Purple needles of 1 crystallized within 1–2 days (approx. 67% yield).",
